  note "The index of the card's people is named people: in tally 2.1, parties is a prelude kind, a built-in id (MIGRATION.md, 2.0 → 2.1; LOAD-DUP otherwise)."
  note "The card gives no dates and moves no money, so its money is written as defs (LANGUAGE 5.10, Places need dates): the flats are keys of an index, each with its value, and ownership is owns[p, f] with stakes in an entity looked through once (3.6). The regime is a key of an index (3.6, N-506)."

source card "Probe card OWN-04 (made up): story and rules"

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01

index flats = [flat_co, flat_comm, flat_est, flat_sep]

index people = [ania, tomek, piotr, ola, halina, marta, kuba, zb_estate]

index regimes = [community, separate, co_owned, in_estate]

input community_part: num

input flat_value[f in flats]: money DUK

input owns[p in people, f in flats]: num

input regime_of[f in flats]: key regimes

input spouse_in[p in people, f in flats]: bool

input stake[p in people, e in people]: num

def part_value[p in people, f in flats]: num DUK = flat_value[f] * share_of[p, f] at reader

def share_of[p in people, f in flats]: num at reader
  note "rule 1: community half to each spouse; separate, co-owned and the estate by their shares"
  rule base v card_rules = owns[p, f] + sum(stake[p, e] * owns[e, f] for e in people)
  rule comm beats base v card_rules = if spouse_in[p, f] then community_part else 0 when regime_of[f] == community

ask q_co_owned: part_value[p, flat_co] for p in [piotr, ola] law 2026-01-01

ask q_community: part_value[p, flat_comm] for p in [ania, tomek] law 2026-01-01

ask q_estate: part_value[p, flat_est] for p in [halina, ania, piotr, marta, kuba] law 2026-01-01

ask q_separate: part_value[p, flat_sep] for p in [ania] law 2026-01-01

