,8:g2/rules,2:g2,18:run g2/rules.tally,1649:14:g2/rules.tally,1625:model g2_rules
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-25
  start 2024-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T, issue #41, G2: rules in force (L §5.11, §4.6): a rule with its own span, rules a later version replaces and replaces again, each read under cuts before and after its version is known, on a version's known day itself, and a rule governing always, read with a law date and, in a def with no at, with none."

source fixture "T's fixture for S's kernel tests (invented values)"

input base_amt: num

input two: num

def r_own: num at reader
  rule base v v_a = base_amt
  rule own beats base v v_a governs 2025-01-01.. = base_amt * two

def r_rep: num at reader
  rule base v v_a = base_amt

def r_always: num at reader
  rule base v v_a = base_amt + two

def r_none: num
  note "no at: it reads nothing law-dated, so it needs no law date"
  rule base v v_a = base_amt - two

ask q_none: r_none

ask q_own_24: r_own law 2024-06-30

ask q_own_25: r_own law 2025-06-30

ask q_rep_24: r_rep law 2024-06-30

ask q_rep_25: r_rep law 2025-06-30

ask q_rep_25_old: r_rep law 2025-06-30 as known 2025-02-01

ask q_rep_25_day: r_rep law 2025-06-30 as known 2025-03-01

ask q_rep_26: r_rep law 2026-06-30

ask q_rep_26_mid: r_rep law 2026-06-30 as known 2025-06-01

ask q_always: r_always law 2026-10-25

version v_a
  cite fixture
  governs always
  known 2024-01-01
  base_amt = 3 "the base amount"
  two = 2 "two"

version v_b
  cite fixture
  governs 2025-01-01..
  known 2025-03-01
  replace rule r_rep.base = base_amt * two

version v_c
  cite fixture
  governs 2026-01-01..
  known 2025-09-01
  replace rule r_rep.base = base_amt * two * two
